      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{610d538d5303a82960a415b4|full_name} Thank you for dropping the old thread. Unfortunately it is outdated, the context is nice. With this email and other things the Shadow Discord Server has discovered officially after the fact, the old saying that VRChat had no control in the matter is outdated. As of today specifically, Epic Games has updated EAC so that Developers can manually opt into allowing their games to run and whitelist on third party services such as ShadowPC and others. \n\nWhile VRChat says its outside of their control, they now have control back. Epic Games implemented something new so that developers themselves can choose whether people who use VMs can play or not.\n\nThank you for your patience. If all of these posts are considered spam, I apologize, our intention was not to cause harm.",
